      {
        "name": "School",
        "content": "<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40/strict.dtd\">\n<html><head><meta name=\"qrichtext\" content=\"1\" /><meta charset=\"utf-8\" /><style type=\"text/css\">\np, li { white-space: pre-wrap; }\nhr { height: 1px; border-width: 0; }\nli.unchecked::marker { content: \"\\2610\"; }\nli.checked::marker { content: \"\\2612\"; }\n</style></head><body style=\" font-family:'Sans Serif'; font-size:11pt; font-weight:400; font-style:normal;\">\n<p style=\" margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;\">Missed coding this morning. I fell asleep at 2am and did not want to wake up that early to go to class. Got an 89% on the exam. That's ok.<br /><br />Felt good with systems analysis. Professor made me feel special when he called on me to not answer any more questions. It was interesting to look back on that. I went to class 10 minutes late due missing coding in the morning.<br /><br />AeroMaterials is a little bit cooked. I need to go back to writing notes and analyzing the class. I was on my laptop most of the class and I got distracted. We watched a nice video. Otherwise it was similar to other days.<br /><br />Wen't to mass after class today. It was nice. It was a smaller area, but a good amount of people showed up. Got may ashes and went to go eat right after class.<br />After I ate I did some work in Retelliata. Worked with Amber on the lab. Apparently it's individual based, so I really did not need to work with him. Kev was also around when I was working. It was very nice talking to him. I was tweaking about data even though it should have been completely fine. We worked for ~2hrs. I was having TOO MANY brain farts while I was working. It was not good. I need to get more sleep so this does not happen. </p></body></html>",
        "created_at": "",
        "tag": "School"
      },
      {
        "name": "Goose",
        "content": "<!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40/strict.dtd\">\n<html><head><meta name=\"qrichtext\" content=\"1\" /><meta charset=\"utf-8\" /><style type=\"text/css\">\np, li { white-space: pre-wrap; }\nhr { height: 1px; border-width: 0; }\nli.unchecked::marker { content: \"\\2610\"; }\nli.checked::marker { content: \"\\2612\"; }\n</style></head><body style=\" font-family:'Sans Serif'; font-size:11pt; font-weight:400; font-style:normal;\">\n<p style=\" margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;\">The Camera works. We just need a lens. At first I was making the CSI port use the wrong board type so I was up late trying to figure that out. After that, I didn't realize we need a lens to make this work. I feel like a real monkey.... I have to decide if we want to get a motorized lens or a manual one. Gonna talk with Schubert about this tmr.<br /><br />Talked with Batu today for 45mins. It was good helping him. I was definetly impatient. I have to get better at being patient with him, but his language barrier was a little tough to get around. He in now working on the project. I will be seeing him tmr to discuss the project more. I have to fix the top model for him and also get the motor asssembly done for him.</p></body></html>",
        "created_at": "",
        "tag": "Goose"
      }
